Content: "Herbert West–Reanimator ""Herbert West–Reanimator"" is a horror short story by American writer H. P. Lovecraft. It was written between October 1921 and June 1922. It was first serialized in February through July 1922 in the amateur publication ""Home Brew"". The story was the basis of the 1985 horror film ""Re-Animator"" and its sequels, in addition to numerous other adaptations in various media. The story is the first to mention Lovecraft's fictional Miskatonic University. It is also one of the first depictions of zombies as scientifically reanimated corpses, with animalistic and uncontrollable temperaments. Lovecraft originally serialised the story in ""Home Brew"""

