Calculate the total number of days the king reigned by applying the alternative method identified in the previous step.
To calculate the total number of days Jehoram of Judah reigned, we need to apply the accession year method. According to the text, Jehoram took the throne at the age of 32 and reigned for 8 years. 

Under the accession year method, the 30 days of the old year are counted as the accession year. Therefore, we need to add 30 days to the 8 years of reign.

8 years * 365.25 days/year (accounting for leap years) = 2920 days
Adding the 30 days of the accession year: 2920 + 30 = 2950 days

So, Jehoram of Judah reigned for approximately 2950 days.
